82 → 5/06/82 (may)\n- 2/11/82 → 5/13/82 (may)\n- 2/18/82 → 5/20/82 (may)\n- 2/25/82 → 5/27/82 (may)\n\nI see a pattern emerging. The bills issued in late February will mature in late May, which doesn't align with the requirement of maturing in the 2nd or 3rd week of June. This means I'll need to dig deeper to find the correct bills.\n\nThe key constraint is the 13-week maturity period. When I calculate from late February 1982, I discover the earliest possible maturity falls in late May or early June. This creates a challenge for finding bills that meet the specific June maturity window.\n\nI'll investigate the 26-week bills to see if they offer a solution to this timing puzzle.\n\nExamining the data reveals several 13-week bills quoted in February that technically mature in May, just before the desired early June timeframe. Specifically, bills issued on 2/04/82, 2/11/82, and 2/18/82 mature in early May, while the 2/25/82 bill reaches maturity at the end of May.\n\nThis suggests I need to adjust my approach or reconsider the interpretation of the original question to find bills that precisely meet the June maturity requirement.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_9bb30e41fa3d48d29f03cec0","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '4375,4395p' /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1982_03.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
